  "body": "Found while refreshing PR #1136 (#543, sinker rough and finish with undersize) over main's #544 (sinker orbit).\n\nWhat happens now: #543's size law (`motion::sinker_undersize::judge`) sizes a rough or finish burn as electrode + 2 x spark gap per axis, and places the tip one undersize above the finished floor. #544's orbit moves the electrode a further `radius` sideways at the burn floor, so an orbited pass burns electrode + 2 x (gap + radius) wide. The law does not count that, so PR #1136 refuses an orbit on a rough or finish by name (`SinkerBurnOp::pass_refusal`, at command creation and at generate) instead of judging it wrongly. A plain single burn may still orbit.\n\nWhat should happen: the common practice is that the electrode undersize per side covers gap + orbit, so a finish with an orbit should be judged as `e + 2(g + r) == c` (a rough: `<= c`), with the floor stand worked out so the floor is neither left short nor over-burned by the orbit, and the stock-sim verdict pinning both.\n\nDone means: a Sinker Burn rough or finish accepts an orbit; `judge` counts the radius in the burned width; a finish with an orbit burns the cavity to size (sim verdict clean, 0 gouge, rest within the sim's resolution); an orbit that would push the walls past the cavity is refused by name; the refusal added in PR #1136 is removed; pins in `sinker_undersize` cover both.\n\nRelated: #543, #544, #547 (electrode from faces subtracts `orbit` in its size: PR #1156).\n",
